WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.601
-Welcome, everybody.
Welcome, welcome, welcome to

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:05.100
"The Tonight Show." You're here.
You made it.

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:07.701
Thank you for being here.
Thank you for watching.

00:00:07.701 --> 00:00:09.200
I am very excited about this.

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:11.868
One of the biggest stars
in the world, Dwayne Johnson,

00:00:11.868 --> 00:00:13.434
is on the show, tonight.

00:00:13.434 --> 00:00:17.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:19.634
I love when Dwayne is here
because there's always a chance

00:00:19.634 --> 00:00:21.267
that he pulls Kevin Hart
out of his pocket.

00:00:21.267 --> 00:00:22.801
It's just -- It's exciting.

00:00:22.801 --> 00:00:25.634
[ Laughter ]

00:00:25.634 --> 00:00:27.801
Yep, Dwayne will be out here
in a little bit,

00:00:27.801 --> 00:00:29.901
or sooner if he wants.
I mean, who's going to stop him?

00:00:29.901 --> 00:00:31.400
You know, he can do
whatever he wants.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:33.300
Let's get to some news first,
guys.

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:35.934
Last night on CNN,
President Biden sat down

00:00:35.934 --> 00:00:38.601
for a prime-time interview with
Jake Tapper.

00:00:38.601 --> 00:00:41.334
At one point, Tapper asked
the President whether his age is

00:00:41.334 --> 00:00:44.501
a concern, and Biden said,
"Not at all, Wolf."

00:00:44.501 --> 00:00:47.567
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.567 --> 00:00:50.400
I think Biden is sick of this
question because he responded,

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:52.834
"I'm so old, I remember
when people watched CNN."

00:00:52.834 --> 00:00:54.667
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.667 --> 00:00:56.267
I got a feeling they're not
going to stop questioning

00:00:56.267 --> 00:00:57.834
Biden's sharpness until he says,

00:00:57.834 --> 00:00:59.767
"Person, woman,
man, camera, TV."

00:00:59.767 --> 00:01:02.100
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:04.334
When they got to the topic of
Russia, Biden said that

00:01:04.334 --> 00:01:06.234
Vladimir Putin totally
miscalculated

00:01:06.234 --> 00:01:07.834
by invading Ukraine.

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:09.501
And I believe him because
if there's one thing

00:01:09.501 --> 00:01:11.400
Biden's an expert on,
it's miscalculating.

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:13.934
-Let me start off
with two words.

00:01:13.934 --> 00:01:15.701
Made in America.

00:01:15.701 --> 00:01:19.234
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.234 --> 00:01:21.400
-Close enough. Who cares?
Two words.

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:25.300
[ Applause ]

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:27.567
Biden also said he has no
intention of meeting with Putin

00:01:27.567 --> 00:01:29.667
at next month's G20 summit.

00:01:29.667 --> 00:01:30.934
Meanwhile, Trump and Putin are

00:01:30.934 --> 00:01:33.167
planning a couple's
Halloween costume.

00:01:33.167 --> 00:01:35.601
"No, Donald, I'm the avocado.
You're the toast."

00:01:35.601 --> 00:01:37.367
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.367 --> 00:01:39.534
Tapper also asked Biden about
the economy

00:01:39.534 --> 00:01:41.200
and where it's headed.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:42.467
Take a look at this.

00:01:42.467 --> 00:01:44.601
-Should the American people
prepare for a recession?

00:01:44.601 --> 00:01:47.133
-No. Look, they've been saying
this now how --

00:01:47.133 --> 00:01:49.267
every six months they say this.

00:01:49.267 --> 00:01:51.400
There's no guarantee that
there's gonna be a rec--

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:53.033
I don't think there will be
a recession.

00:01:53.033 --> 00:01:55.167
If it is, it will be
a very slight recession.

00:01:55.167 --> 00:01:58.701
[ Laughter ]

00:01:58.701 --> 00:02:00.434
-A slight recession? Yeah.

00:02:00.434 --> 00:02:01.901
I wouldn't invite someone
to a party

00:02:01.901 --> 00:02:03.267
if you told me
they had a smidge of COVID.

00:02:03.267 --> 00:02:04.300
Do you know what I'm saying?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:06.434
Just a little bit.

00:02:06.434 --> 00:02:07.734
Some big entertainment news,
guys.

00:02:07.734 --> 00:02:09.467
Our good friend Blake Shelton,
just announced that

00:02:09.467 --> 00:02:11.901
after next season
he's leaving "The Voice."

00:02:11.901 --> 00:02:13.367
[ Audience aws ]

00:02:13.367 --> 00:02:15.501
Yep, Blake is stepping away from
his chair so he can go home

00:02:15.501 --> 00:02:17.434
and spend more time
in his chair.

00:02:17.434 --> 00:02:19.100
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:21.467
And finally, guys, there's a lot
going on in the news right now,

00:02:21.467 --> 00:02:22.968
but instead of me just telling
you about it,

00:02:22.968 --> 00:02:24.200
I thought it would be nice to
give you the chance

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:25.534
to decide what we talk about.

00:02:25.534 --> 00:02:27.667
That's right, it's time for
"You Pick the Joke."

00:02:27.667 --> 00:02:30.300
Here we go.
-♪ Joke ♪

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:32.767
♪ You pick the joke ♪

00:02:32.767 --> 00:02:34.801
-So, here's how it works.
I'm going to show you two news

00:02:34.801 --> 00:02:37.133
stories, then you guys get to
pick which one we talk about.

00:02:37.133 --> 00:02:39.434
Here we go. Let's take a look at
story number one.

00:02:39.434 --> 00:02:41.601
-Gas prices are on the rise
in the U.S.

00:02:41.601 --> 00:02:45.434
and could soon hit the national
average of $4 a gallon.

00:02:45.434 --> 00:02:48.167
-Mm. Here's story number two.

00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:51.000
-A bizarre story out of
Westmoreland County tonight.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:54.901
-Police say a man took off all
his clothes and started eating

00:02:54.901 --> 00:02:57.901
vegetables out of people's
backyard gardens.

00:02:57.901 --> 00:02:59.701
[ Laughter ]
-Alright.

00:02:59.701 --> 00:03:02.000
Which story do you want to talk
about, one or two?

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:03.734
-Two!
-Two.

00:03:03.734 --> 00:03:06.033
Okay, alright. Good choice.

00:03:06.033 --> 00:03:07.501
That's right.
-Oh, my God.

00:03:07.501 --> 00:03:10.801
-A naked guy was in people's
gardens eating their vegetables.

00:03:10.801 --> 00:03:13.701
Homeowners were like,
"Honey, is that a string bean

00:03:13.701 --> 00:03:16.767
in the cucumber patch?"
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:16.767 --> 00:03:18.467
-That's nuts.

00:03:20.467 --> 00:03:23.067
-Let's try another story
up here. It's up to you.

00:03:23.067 --> 00:03:24.334
Here's story number one.

00:03:24.334 --> 00:03:27.367
-The Nobel Prize in economic
sciences was awarded

00:03:27.367 --> 00:03:29.501
to three U.S.-based economists.

00:03:29.501 --> 00:03:31.467
-Alright.
Here's story number two.

00:03:31.467 --> 00:03:33.534
-There is new video of a failed
robbery attempt

00:03:33.534 --> 00:03:35.300
at a fast-food restaurant.

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:36.801
According to Houston police,

00:03:36.801 --> 00:03:41.167
the suspect told the employees
this was his first robbery.

00:03:41.167 --> 00:03:45.734
He had a change of heart,
and then he leaves empty-handed.

00:03:45.734 --> 00:03:47.534
-Yeah.
Want to talk about one or two?

00:03:47.534 --> 00:03:49.801
-Two!
-Great choice. That's right.

00:03:49.801 --> 00:03:52.534
First-time robber changed
his mind about the robbery.

00:03:52.534 --> 00:03:54.434
He was like, "Give me all
your money, or not!

00:03:54.434 --> 00:03:55.968
Either way, I just hope we can
be friends."

00:03:55.968 --> 00:03:57.667
[ Laughter ]
"I just want to be friends.

00:03:57.667 --> 00:03:59.100
It's just --
We have a lot in common."

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:01.367
[ Applause ]

00:04:01.367 --> 00:04:02.767
Alright.
Let's do one last batch.

00:04:02.767 --> 00:04:04.467
It's your choice.
Here's story number one.

00:04:04.467 --> 00:04:07.133
-There is a renewed possibility
of a rail strike

00:04:07.133 --> 00:04:09.634
after the country's third
largest railroad union

00:04:09.634 --> 00:04:11.133
rejected a labor deal.

00:04:11.133 --> 00:04:12.901
-And here's story number two.

00:04:12.901 --> 00:04:16.701
-A nursing home in Taiwan is
apologizing after hiring

00:04:16.701 --> 00:04:19.601
a stripper to perform
for senior citizens.

00:04:19.601 --> 00:04:21.567
-Want to talk about one or talk
about story number two?

00:04:21.567 --> 00:04:22.767
-Two!
-Alright, perfect.

00:04:22.767 --> 00:04:24.133
That's a great choice.
That's right.

00:04:24.133 --> 00:04:26.868
They brought in strippers
to a nursing home.

00:04:26.868 --> 00:04:29.300
The seniors loved it.
It was the first time anyone

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:30.767
made it rain with
nickels and pennies.

00:04:30.767 --> 00:04:32.634
There you go.
That was "You Pick the Joke."

00:04:32.634 --> 00:04:33.634
We have a great show.

